# Normalize line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Why this exists: this project is edited from both Windows and macOS, and
# QLC+ rewrites the whole .qxw on every save using platform line endings.
# Normalization currently happens to work because this machine's
# core.autocrlf handles it, but that is per-machine config, not a property
# of the repo - a clone on a differently-configured machine would start
# committing CRLF and turn every one-scene change into a whole-file diff.
#
# With `text` set here, Git normalizes CRLF -> LF on `git add` regardless of
# local config, so it no longer matters what QLC+ or a Mac editor wrote.

* text=auto

# QLC+ workspaces and fixture definitions are XML - always text.
*.qxw text
*.qxf text

# Wavefront OBJ/MTL are ASCII.
*.obj text
*.mtl text

# GDTF is a ZIP container; Blender scenes and renders are binary.
*.gdtf binary
*.blend binary
*.blend1 binary
*.ply  binary
*.glb  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
